          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "எழுதுங்கள் (eḻutuṅkaḷ) — \"please write (it)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It shares its root with எழுத்து, \"a letter of the script\". இங்கே எழுதுங்கள் (eḻutuṅkaḷ) — \"please write it here\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "எழுதுங்கள் (eḻutuṅkaḷ) is native Dravidian. DEDR 853 lists Malayalam eḻutuka. The ending -uṅkaḷ makes it a polite request."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
